Both \(t=2\) controls come out correctly: the \(y=1/5\) cone has dimension one and \(\tau\) is already in the ideal; the \(y=2/5\) cone has dimension zero. At \(t=3,4\), exact arithmetic gives \(\tau\notin I_{t,+}\) but \(\tau^2\in I_{t,+}\). At \(t=4\), the square does **not** belong to the top-tail ideal alone, so that stronger shortcut fails.
