The report draft contains the full Abel equivalence and its reconstruction proof. Exact checks also rule out another shortcut: at \(t=4\), \(\tau\notin I_{t,+}+(b_3)\), despite \(\tau^2\in I_{t,+}\). Using all positive rows, the enlarged matrix’s minors alone prove cone finiteness at \(t=3,4\). I’m auditing the draft while the two \(t=8\) jobs approach their time limits.
